> [38;2;255;255;255mIn the terminal tab loading state logic we need to make a change. IN normal sessions we start the state as 'Connected' And don't Enter 'Loading/Thinkin' [m[K[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;55;55;55m
 until the uer hits enter for the forst time. But for sessions we resume. i.e click a chat history->send to->CLI we need to start in a 'Loading/Thinking'  [m[K[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;55;55;55m
state until they hit the first Idel event and the put them in Ready Until the user hots Enter. First Idel event, then stay 'Ready' until Enter is what we  [m[K[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;55;55;55m
have already os it's just the starting logic that has to change, and only for chat's that have been resumed.[47X[m[47C[K
